  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 579,
   "id": "f149fb3e-efda-4e56-b56a-ff5cc372913f",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "#plot_all_data(PD_IDX, quantile_alpha=0.01, save_path='log_likelihood')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "5050a425-a90f-4b4f-92db-c0f97aa5b9f8",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "We cut off at a certain quantile. <br>\n",
    "\"prior\" is the N(0,1) with the respective dimensionality - not visible prior lines are intended as they would distort the plot<br>\n",
    "\"true\" is the true distribution - not that it different to the prior as most of it comes from: N(0,var)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "00305a84-721f-4c92-9b96-51049426d37f",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "#### Working Deflation\n",
    "\n",
    "$\\int q(x) dx = \\int q(x) \\frac{p(x)}{p(x)} dx \\approx \\frac{1}{N} \\sum \\frac{q(x)}{p(x)}$ <br>\n",
    "$\\int \\left( \\sum \\frac{q(x)}{p(x)} \\right)^{-1} q(x) dx \\approx 1$ <br>\n",
    "exp_vals = q - true_p\n",
    "logged_norm_const = - np.log(len(exp_vals)) + logsumexp(exp_vals)\n",
    "return q - logged_norm_const"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 580,
   "id": "cdfe4004-7237-4fbc-85bc-b195b2d937dc",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "#%matplotlib qt / inline\n",
